{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-system.txt clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-closing.txt clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-schema.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-system.txt clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-closing.txt clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c19-schema.json'","aggregated_output":"ROLE\n\nYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst reading one source item for the company in scope (current_entity); \"the company\" below is that\ncompany. The research already tracked for it is listed in open_theses. Your first job is evidence: decide by the rules below which\nstatements in the item are material, then link each one to every thesis it informs: an open thesis that covers it, a new thesis you\npropose, or both. Your second job is new theses: the important research questions this item raises that no open thesis\ncovers. Every new thesis comes with evidence from this item. A material statement that no open thesis covers and that is not\nitself a big matter (section 3) is returned with empty links: code keeps it in the company's record without links and links it\nwhen a thesis that covers it opens. Never open a thesis only to give a statement a home.\n\nINPUT\n\n- current_entity and company_tags: the company in scope and the companies the item is tagged with. Code assigns the entity; do not\n  invent one. Evidence can describe another party when it informs research on the company.\n- open_theses: the identity, question, tracked outcome and period of each thesis already tracked. They tell you where evidence belongs\n  and whether an idea is already covered; they are not evidence. You do not see the evidence already stored; a later step compares\n  new evidence with history.\n- source_item: the complete text and its source metadata.\n\n1. EVIDENCE: WHAT TO KEEP\n\n- A material statement is one of four kinds. (1) The company's own figure, guidance or decision: \"same-store sales rose 4.2% in the\n  quarter\"; \"management guided full-year revenue to $12–13 billion\"; \"the board approved a $10 billion buyback\". (2) A customer's,\n  supplier's, competitor's or partner's action or reported figure with a size, date or name that bears on the company's demand,\n  supply, input costs, competition, prices or products: \"the largest customer said it will cut orders by a fifth next year\"; \"a bank\n  chose a rival's system\"; \"a software firm is integrating the company's model into its government systems\"; \"the main supplier said\n  its capacity will double by 2027\"; \"a rival cut list prices 15% in Europe\"; \"the largest customer reported its order backlog doubled\n  to $40 billion\". An action is a step the item reports as news: taken, decided or planned (an order, a contract, a selection, an\n  integration under way, an expansion, a cut, a price change, a deployment plan). A party that already uses, hosts, runs or has built\n  on the company's products, and the benefits it describes from that use (faster, cheaper, more accurate), describe an arrangement in\n  place, which is background; its own revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amounts are figures under (2) (\"a hospital chain uses\n  the company's scheduling software and reports shorter waits\"). (3) A named party's new claim or estimate about the company or its\n  industry, with or without a figure, whether an analyst, a customer's or rival's executive or an official makes it: \"the CFO said\n  plants built a decade ago still run at full capacity\"; \"an analyst raised next year's EPS estimate to $4.10\"; \"an analyst said the\n  bank's loan losses next quarter will come in well above consensus\"; \"a short seller accused the company of overstating receivables\n  by $2 billion\". (4) A policy or regulatory decision or\n  step, including one still in force that the item reports: \"the regulator approved the drug for a second indication\"; \"the\n  government required licences for exports of the product\"; \"the regulator still bars sales of the drug in the country\".\n- Go through the item from its first paragraph to its last, including paragraphs about matters other than the headline. The four\n  kinds describe what material statements usually look like; they do not decide what is kept. Take a statement when an analyst\n  following the company would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely, and no row\n  of the closing check at the end of this request rejects it; a row's \"it does not cover\" clause sends the statement back to that test\n  and keeps it only where the row says so. Most of an item is background, but a page with eight statements that pass yields eight\n  evidence items, not a selection.\n\n2. LINK EACH STATEMENT TO ITS THESES\n\n- EXISTING: if an open thesis covers the statement, link it to that thesis's exact supplied ID, including contrary facts. Do not\n  return or rename the thesis's description.\n- NEW: if the statement raises a research question that merits separate tracking and no open or newly proposed thesis covers it,\n  propose a thesis (section 3) and link the statement to it.\n- NO THESIS YET: if no open or newly proposed thesis covers a statement you judge material, and the matter is not big enough by\n  its own scale to merit a thesis (section 3), return it with empty links; it is kept without links.\n- CONDITION: a statement of the company's own financial figures (a reported result or balance, its guidance, or a named party's\n  or consensus estimate) lists its useful figures in figures. Its results, guidance and estimates, margins included, inform an open thesis about its revenue or earnings\n  path when they bear on that path; a different period is not on its own a reason to leave them unlinked. When no open or new\n  thesis covers it, its links stay empty. A figure is useful when it can change what an analyst\n  expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position: a retailer's quarterly\n  same-store sales, an airline's guidance for next year's unit costs and analysts' consensus earnings for a bank are; a cash-rich\n  company's cash balance or cash flow usually changes none of these when the item ties it to nothing, while a heavily indebted\n  firm's cash burn changes its credit risk. The share price, a target price and other companies' figures are never conditions.\n- Link one statement to every thesis it informs, and to none that its own relevance says it does not inform; use the narrowest\n  relevant thesis only when choosing between theses that cover the same thing.\n- Match by the underlying question or outcome, subject and scope, and time when relevant, not by word overlap. A different wording,\n  source, forecast or direction alone does not make a new thesis. Related questions can be separate when their outcomes matter\n  independently.\n- Do not exclude evidence solely because it concerns a related period, population or product variant. Assess whether it can inform\n  the open question, preserving the difference in the record. Do not present a forecast for a later year as a forecast for the\n  thesis's year. If another open thesis covers the evidence more directly, consider that thesis as well; do not assume different\n  periods are automatically the same thesis or automatically unrelated.\n\nExamples of linking evidence to research:\n\n- Supply chain: an open thesis asks whether a manufacturer's production is constrained. A named supplier announces a capacity\n  expansion for a component the manufacturer uses. Link the announcement as a potential supply signal; it does not establish\n  allocations or deliveries.\n- Geopolitics: an open thesis asks whether an exporter can sell in a specified market. The relevant government proposes a licensing\n  restriction on that product. Link the proposal as evidence about market access; a proposal is not an enacted restriction.\n- Macro: an open thesis asks whether a company's borrowing costs will rise. The item reports that its floating-rate debt is tied to a\n  benchmark that has risen. Link the benchmark movement and the stated exposure; do not calculate the expense change unless the\n  source supports it.\n- Competition: an open thesis asks whether a company can retain customers in a product market. A named competitor cuts the price of a\n  competing product. Link the price cut as competitive evidence; do not assert lost customers or share without support.\n\n3. WHEN TO PROPOSE A NEW THESIS\n\nA thesis is a question a senior analyst would hold a card for: its answer could change a position because it could change the\ncompany's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk, or competitive position in a way you can name; public material will settle it on a\ndate; and no open thesis already asks it. A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event. It opens for one of four reasons, a closed set; a matter that fits none of them is\nevidence, kept and linked to the theses it informs or left unlinked, never a thesis:\n- product_node: when the generation of the main product that carries the company's value reaches the step that brings revenue,\n  usually first shipments; announcements and samples are its evidence, and only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's\n  trial result and its approval) are separate theses (\"will the carmaker's new platform start deliveries in 2026?\";\n  \"will the drugmaker's next-generation inhaler, the product line that carries its value, reach pharmacies by mid-2027?\").\n- binding_obligation: an obligation the company takes on in its own name, large enough to change its revenue, profit, cash or credit\n  risk: guaranteeing, backing or giving credit support for another party's debt, lease, revenue or capacity, lending to it,\n  committing to buy capacity or services, or a sized stake or acquisition not yet completed. One already undertaken is tracked by its\n  amount at the next annual report; one not yet signed by whether it is signed by a check date within 18 months of the item (\"how much will the\n  utility have guaranteed for its project companies' loans at its next annual report?\"; \"will the retailer sign a guarantee for its\n  franchisees' leases, large enough to change its credit risk, by the check date?\"). Its own borrowing or leases and a completed\n  or unsized investment are not obligations.\n- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\n  several companies' combined output or spending, a contract price, an interest rate (\"the largest container lines' combined capacity\n  added in 2026\"; \"next year's average contract price of a raw material\"). Another population or wording of the same aggregate is\n  evidence for it.\n- policy_stage: the step a policy or regulatory process reaches, naming who decides (\"will the regulator approve the drug for a second\n  indication?\"; \"will the government require licences for the product's exports by a date?\").\n\n- Open only matters an analyst would bet on separately; small matters open no thesis and their statements are kept as evidence. A\n  customer's deployment plan is evidence for the company's demand and product theses, unless it changes the company's own cash or\n  credit risk, which is judged as an obligation.\n- Give the date the item supports. When it gives none, use the date the reason fixes and say how it was set: an obligation already\n  undertaken, its next annual report; an unsigned obligation, a check date within 18 months of the item; a pending regulatory\n  decision, the current fiscal year-end. A shared quantity takes its release date and a product event the date its outcome can be\n  checked, only when the item supports one. A question no date can settle is rewritten or not opened.\n- Do not open a thesis about: an executive appointment or organisational change; the company's own borrowing or leases as an\n  obligation; a buyback authorisation or dividend declaration; a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for any period,\n  on its own; an undated moat or strategy; a feature, content or software update, price point, regional service or variant of a\n  product already on sale; another estimate, source or wording of what an open thesis tracks; an annual quantity after next year (an\n  obligation excepted); shareholder votes, bylaws or routine litigation procedure. Their statements are evidence for the theses they\n  inform, or left unlinked.\n- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\n  open thesis with why an analyst would bet on the two separately because their answers can move apart; with no open thesis, say so.\n  If the two cannot move apart, link the evidence to every open thesis it informs instead.\n\nCounterexamples:\n\n- \"The company's outlook is interesting\" or \"the industry may change\" is too vague: it names no outcome later evidence can inform.\n- If an open thesis tracks sales growth, a revised sales forecast is evidence for it; do not open a second thesis to repeat it.\n- A customer expanding capacity informs demand; it is not a thesis of its own, and not a claim that the supplier has received orders.\n- \"Is the stock attractively valued?\" is an investment conclusion, not a research question about the business.\n\n4. HOW TO WRITE EVIDENCE\n\n- One evidence item records one statement, and that statement is what you judge: a figure, date or comparison in the neighbouring\n  words does not make another claim in the same passage new or material. A statement told in several sentences of the item, with its\n  terms, figures and conditions, is one item.\n- Write a standalone summary: who did or said what, how much and for which period, naming the measure even when a neighbouring\n  sentence gives it. Preserve conditions, uncertainty and attribution. Return every passage the summary rests on, each copied\n  verbatim and contiguously from the item, without translation; do not join distant passages with an ellipsis.\n- Name the actor in the summary and identify the original party whose action, figure or claim it is. Give the reporting speaker when\n  available. The item's publisher and publication date come from its source metadata.\n- Use only this item's information. Distinguish forecasts, allegations and unconfirmed reports from confirmed outcomes. Report plans\n  as plans; do not infer committed funding, orders, deliveries or revenue.\n- For each item, return its evidence tier, the original statement date and the period the statement describes. These are separate\n  pieces of information.\n\nEVIDENCE TIER\n\nClassify the statement by what is confirmed, not how important it is:\n\n- rumour: the item attributes the claim to unnamed sources or calls it unconfirmed.\n- fact: an official action, published actual figure or completed transaction, including an announcement or completed transaction\n  reported by an article.\n- party_statement: a company's guidance, management statement or official's remarks. A forecast is a statement, not a completed\n  outcome.\n- third_party_view: an analyst's, journalist's or expert's opinion or estimate.\n\nApply the first matching category in that order. An unnamed-source or unconfirmed claim remains a rumour even if it describes an\naction or number. If none matches and the claim is unattributed, use rumour. The tier is not an importance score.\n\nEVIDENCE TIME\n\n- statement_date: the original statement's full day in YYYY-MM-DD when known; otherwise null. Do not use the article date as the\n  original date unless the statement was made in the originating party's own release, filing, call or analysis. Do not assign that\n  date to an older statement quoted there.\n- statement_date_text: the original date or partial date as stated, if present; otherwise null. Preserve a month or relative date\n  without inventing a day. A forecast horizon or an occasion is not a date.\n- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\n  statement date.\n\nReturn the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nlists when nothing passes.\nBefore you return the answer, check it once. Read each evidence item back as the analyst following the company and keep it when you would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely, about the company or its customers, suppliers, competitors, regulators or the economy. Ask first whether it is new: repeated common knowledge, a long-standing situation retold and an unargued view are noise. Do not drop a reported step, figure, guidance, forecast or decision because the item retells it or another outlet reported it before: a later step compares each statement with the evidence already stored and records a repeat there. Guidance, a forecast, a plan or a decision still in force keeps its place even when retold, including a change to a plan, design or schedule that another outlet reported days or weeks before. Judge the action or information itself, not its verb tense, and do not take a statement as old because its date is missing. Fitting one of the four kinds does not keep an item. A missing amount, date or scale never drops an item on its own: a forecast, a rumour, a counter-example or a distant or conditional statement is judged like any other.\nThese are not kept, even when a named party states them. What a row says it does not cover goes back to the test above, unless the row says it is kept:\n- background the analyst already knew, such as the company's history (\"the company was founded in 1998\"); an arrangement the item only describes as in place, even when no date is given: customers or partners that use, host, run or have built on the company's products, and the benefits they describe from that use (\"two airlines fly the planemaker's jets\"; \"three insurers run claims on the company's software and report faster payouts\"); a partnership, contract, plant or investment the item itself dates to an earlier month or year with no new step (\"earlier this year the company partnered with the glassmaker on three plants\"; \"in May it signed a $3 billion cloud contract\"); it does not cover a step the item reports as news, taken, decided, planned or under way (an order, a selection, an integration, an expansion, a deployment), even when it gives no date (\"the retailer's largest supplier is opening its own stores, people familiar said this week\"; \"the two largest cement makers are adding kilns to meet demand\"), nor a customer's, supplier's or partner's newly disclosed revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amount; a deal the item mentions as already existing is an arrangement in place even with its amount (\"a rival airline already leases 40 of the same jets\");\n- a typical claim that is common knowledge, without a figure and a specific account: that a firm leads or competes, that demand is strong or supply tight, a general risk (\"if demand slows it would hurt\"); a number does not lift a familiar position (\"the rival grocer has led this market for years and still holds 40%\"); it does not cover a dated forecast of a shortage, a price or demand (\"the steelmaker expects the shortage to peak next year and last until 2028\"), a competitor's newly reported share, volume or price in the company's market (\"the local rival now holds about half of the regional market, worth about $5 billion\"), nor a reported movement of a named price, rental rate, lead time or order book, even without a figure (\"rental rates for used trucks have been climbing this quarter\"); a general statement that demand stays strong or a product stays popular is not one;\n- a product, game, driver or benchmark specification with no business scale (\"the vacuum runs 60 minutes on a charge\"; \"a benchmark score\"), a retail price detail (\"a retailer marks one model down by $50\"), and a comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes (\"the maker says its drug works twice as fast as older ones\"; \"a reviewer's test\"); it does not cover a competitor's comparison against the company's product, a partner's or customer's adoption or integration (also when a comparison shares its sentence), a reported launch, shipment, delay or cancellation of any of the company's products or a change to a product plan or configuration, including a reported sign that a planned product is going ahead (\"the long-range version of the jet is likely delayed or limited to a few deliveries\"; \"a parts supplier's catalogue lists the unannounced model\"), nor the company's decision to change the price it charges; uncertainty or a smaller product line does not make it a specification;\n- an unargued view or a quote that only characterises (\"the stock is a hold\"; \"a pivotal moment\"; \"an industry-leading platform\"), and a named analyst's reading of an event already recorded that adds no new fact or calculation (\"the recall shows quality risks are rising\"); it does not cover a reading that adds a new fact or calculation, nor the company's own statement that its plan, schedule or guidance still stands (\"the carmaker said the launch date has not moved\"), which is judged as the plan itself would be; a target price or valuation of the company is not kept, even with its assumptions and derivation, while the estimates it rests on are judged on their own (an analysts' earnings forecast is kept);\n- a political or strategic stance with no figure and no decision (\"diversifying suppliers will not reduce dependence\"); it does not cover a policy or regulatory step, nor a decision still in force that the item reports;\n- a share-price move, an investor's position or trade, or the market value (\"shares fell 13% this month\"; \"he is short the stock\"); it does not cover the news behind the move;\n- another company's matter that touches none of the company's markets (its valuation, share price, governance or a deal outside them), or that sits next to the company only by sharing an article, an event or an ecosystem; you supply the connection as the analyst and the item need not state it: a customer's spending, orders or backlog bears on demand, a supplier's capacity, output, prices or revenue on supply and input costs, a rival's products, prices or share in the company's markets on competition (\"a large customer's order backlog doubled\"; \"the main supplier's quarterly revenue jumped on demand for the part\");\n- the same fact said again in other words within this item: one deal, hire, programme or reported measure told in several sentences, with its terms, figures and growth rates, is one evidence item; keep the fuller wording (\"a $2 billion order for 120 stores in 15 countries over three years\"; \"cloud revenue of $8 billion, up 30% on the year and 6% on the quarter, 40% of the total\"); a deal one party signs under a wider programme, with its own amount or capacity, is its own evidence item, and a fact another outlet reported before is not a repeat within this item;\n- company boilerplate, bylines, forward-looking-statement text.\nA report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\nReturn only the evidence items you keep.\nThen check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\nFor each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\nAn item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n{\n \"type\": \"object\",\n \"additionalProperties\": false,\n \"required\": [\n  \"new_theses\",\n  \"evidence\"\n ],\n \"properties\": {\n  \"new_theses\": {\n   \"type\": \"array\",\n   \"description\": \"New thesis proposals, each referenced by at least one evidence link.\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n     \"local_id\",\n     \"description\",\n     \"outcome\",\n     \"period\",\n     \"settles_on\",\n     \"outcomes\",\n     \"opens_as\",\n     \"settled_by\",\n     \"closest_open_thesis\",\n     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n     \"local_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Local reference for this new thesis in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n     },\n     \"description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The proposed research question, stated clearly.\"\n     },\n     \"outcome\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The outcome or event being tracked by this thesis.\"\n     },\n     \"period\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The period or check date that settles the thesis: the one the item supports, or the one its reason fixes (section 3), with how it was set.\"\n     },\n     \"settles_on\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\",\n      \"description\": \"What settles this thesis: one quantity for one period, which may be its change against a stated earlier period (a calendar year against the year before), or one event checked by a date (whether it has happened by then). If no date and public material can place the answer in fixed outcomes, rewrite the thesis; if it cannot be rewritten, do not propose it (whether its statements are kept is judged as evidence, section 4).\"\n     },\n     \"outcomes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 2,\n      \"maxItems\": 5,\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n       \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\"\n      },\n      \"description\": \"This thesis's fixed outcomes, written now: five ranges of that quantity or of its change, or the event's states, five or two (two for a yes/no, such as whether an unsigned deal is signed by the check date); checkable, not overlapping and leaving no gap, so that exactly one holds on the check date; a middle range says what it is compared with. A company thesis's outcomes describe the business result, even when a policy drives it; a theme's (a quantity or event in the world rather than one company's result) describe only the result, not whether it is good.\"\n     },\n     \"opens_as\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n       \"product_node\",\n       \"binding_obligation\",\n       \"shared_quantity\",\n       \"policy_stage\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The reason this thesis opens, one of the four in section 3.\"\n     },\n     \"settled_by\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The public material that will settle the answer on a date (a filing, an official decision, a shipment confirmation, a statistics release).\",\n      \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\"\n     },\n     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Exact ID of the open thesis closest to this one; null when the open list is empty.\"\n     },\n     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Why an analyst would bet on this question separately from the closest open thesis: how their answers can move apart.\"\n     }\n    }\n   }\n  },\n  \"evidence\": {\n   \"type\": \"array\",\n   \"description\": \"Evidence statements extracted from this item, with their thesis links.\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n     \"local_id\",\n     \"summary\",\n     \"source_passages\",\n     \"original_party\",\n     \"reporting_speaker\",\n     \"tier\",\n     \"statement_date\",\n     \"statement_date_text\",\n     \"evidence_period\",\n     \"links\",\n     \"figures\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n     \"local_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Local reference for this evidence in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n     },\n     \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Standalone faithful summary naming the actor and preserving relevant figures, periods and conditions.\"\n     },\n     \"source_passages\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"description\": \"Contiguous verbatim passages from this source item that jointly support the summary; return each passage separately.\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n     },\n     \"original_party\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Party whose action, figure or claim is reported; null if unknown. Use the reporting outlet or author as the original party only for its own estimate, analysis or unnamed-source report.\"\n     },\n     \"reporting_speaker\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Person or outlet making or reporting the statement in this item, when known; null if unknown.\"\n     },\n     \"statement_date\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"pattern\": \"^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original statement day as YYYY-MM-DD when known; null if the full day is unknown.\"\n     },\n     \"figures\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"additionalProperties\": false,\n       \"required\": [\n        \"measure\",\n        \"period\",\n        \"value\",\n        \"kind\",\n        \"basis\"\n       ],\n       \"properties\": {\n        \"measure\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"The financial measure as the passage states it.\"\n        },\n        \"period\": {\n         \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n           \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n           \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"The period as stated; null when none is given.\"\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"The figure copied exactly from one of this item's passages, with its unit.\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"enum\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"guidance\",\n          \"estimate\"\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"actual: reported, including a balance as of a date; guidance: the company's own outlook; estimate: a named party's or consensus forecast.\"\n        },\n        \"basis\": {\n         \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n           \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n           \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"Scope and qualifications as stated (GAAP or non-GAAP, segment or company, conditions); null when none.\"\n        }\n       }\n      },\n      \"description\": \"The company's own useful financial figures this statement states (section 2, CONDITION); empty for any other statement. A statement with several useful figures stays one item and lists them all.\"\n     },\n     \"links\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 0,\n      \"description\": \"The existing or proposed theses this evidence informs; empty when it is material but no thesis takes it yet: it is kept in the company's record and linked when a covering thesis opens.\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"additionalProperties\": false,\n       \"required\": [\n        \"target_type\",\n        \"target_id\",\n        \"relevance\"\n       ],\n       \"properties\": {\n        \"target_type\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"enum\": [\n          \"existing\",\n          \"new\"\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"Whether the reference identifies an open thesis or a new proposal.\"\n        },\n        \"target_id\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"Exact supplied ID when existing, or local_id of a new thesis in this answer.\"\n        },\n        \"relevance\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"How this evidence informs the referenced thesis, distinguishing source claims from inference.\"\n        }\n       }\n      }\n     },\n     \"tier\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n       \"fact\",\n       \"party_statement\",\n       \"third_party_view\",\n       \"rumour\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Source tier of the statement; an unconfirmed or unnamed-source claim takes precedence as rumour.\"\n     },\n     \"statement_date_text\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original date or partial date as stated in the item; null when absent.\"\n     },\n     \"evidence_period\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Period the fact, plan or forecast describes, as supported by the item; null when unknown.\"\n     }\n    }\n   }\n  }\n }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D417|问题怎么写|开题|开题理由|结果|§3|§4' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D417|问题怎么写|开题|开题理由|结果|§3|§4' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:3:<title>Hivemind 抽取与开题标准</title>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:130:    <li><a href=\"#opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</a></li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:145:  <h1>抽取与开题标准</h1>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:154:  <dd>一个在追这家公司的分析员读到会记进本周笔记的陈述，就留；留下以后另判分量<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2、§4</span>。整体倾向谨慎：杂音很大，不是什么都要抽，不是什么都算线索；但新信息带来的增量要敏感，不能漏<span class=\"src\">D243</span>。预测、传闻、反证、远期、条件情景都可以是证据，不因为\"还没发生\"\"不是官方\"\"离现在远\"\"和我们方向相反\"就不留<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>。有名有姓的动作缺金额、缺日期也照留，分量可以低一点<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。泛泛的主张和背景是常识，没有数字和具体的叙事就不收<span class=\"src\">D243</span>。</dd>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:155:  <dt>开题</dt>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:194:<tr><td>2</td><td>\"共同量\"按 D191 落实：任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格（合计支出、合约价、利率）都可以开题，开题理由叫 <code>shared_quantity</code>；期间按自然年。提示词和代码要跟着改</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 3 节 D 类</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:208:<p>Alex 逐个听了例子、逐个选的，七个都选 A；改了第 2、3、4 节，标准升为第 4 版，金标要按第 4 版重推：开题部分逐条重判，证据部分逐条核对（D244）。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:213:<tr><td>1</td><td>同一个计划的几种说法，最后核对同一个数的，是一题；各自会变、会分别盯的数才分开；属于已按金额开题的计划的一笔交易并进去</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:214:<tr><td>2</td><td>同一件事的不同截止日：早的那题开着时，晚的截止日是它的证据；早的到期没有结果、事情还在追，系统开下一个截止日的续期题，带上证据，不等新文章</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:216:<tr><td>4</td><td>公司自己的量只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:218:<tr><td>6</td><td>单笔交易、产品、项目，规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开题；够不上的不开题，它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判，留下的是证据</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 3 节 C 类、第 4 节</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:233:<p>尺子跟着修：金标的证据部分按第 5 版重推、另存冻结，打分程序遇到证据部分版本对不上就拒绝打分；开题部分重推之前不报开题的分（第 8 节）。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:250:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">问题（观点）</td><td>账本里追踪的一件事：一个问题句、一组结果档、一个到期日，写下后不改<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span></td><td></td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:252:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">标的问题、主题问题</td><td>标的：答案是一家可交易公司（或币、商品）自己的经营结果。主题：答案是世界上的一件事，影响很多公司<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span></td><td></td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:253:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">开题理由</td><td>候选问题值得开的几类理由之一，答案里写在 <code>opens_as</code><span class=\"src\">D184；英文 admission reason</span></td><td></td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:254:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">结果档</td><td>一个问题事先固定、互不重叠、覆盖全部结果的结局，五档或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06；英文 rung</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:256:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">分量</td><td>一条证据对判断有多重要：核心、辅助、可选、不收<span class=\"src\">第 6 节；D243</span>。Alex 说的\"档位低一点\"指它</td><td>结果档、来源层</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:266:<li><b>问题</b>问题句、结果档、到期日写下不改；当前判断随证据更新，到期定格<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。问题分标的和主题，按开题理由分五类（第 3 节）。问题从三处来：文章里的候选问题；用户的备忘录<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 State</span>：\"A thesis from the user's memo is not yet judged until evidence first links to it\"；分析员开始覆盖一家公司时种下的驱动问题<span class=\"src\">D208，设计未建</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:267:<li><b>研究组</b>一件正在进行的事（一个产品换代及其部署、一笔融资或收购、一个政策过程、一轮投资或需求周期），把几个问题组织在一起，常常跨公司。它不是问题，也不代替开题判断。公司自己的报表行（收入、毛利率、费用、税率、资本开支）不带研究组，除非这一行本身就在追这样一件事；它也可以加入别的问题建的组<span class=\"src\">D165</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:269:<p><b>不进账本的：</b>归档找不到家的证据，记 <code>no home</code> 扔掉<span class=\"src\">D209</span>。评估时逐条读被扔的，分四种：抽取的垃圾；库里缺这个问题（覆盖缺口）；问题在却没挂上（归档错）；该开没开（开题错）。各归各的环节<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §7</span>。存储的表结构归 PRD 06 管。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:272:<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:274:<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:277:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:278:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:296:<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:297:<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:300:<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:304:<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:305:<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:308:<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:309:<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:310:<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:315:<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318:<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:337:<tr><td>以约束性义务为理由开：公司自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。它们不是约束性义务；对别的问题仍可以是证据，或按别的开题理由判</td><td>D236、D238</td><td>证据</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:345:<li><b>总规则：</b>同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题；答案能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注的，才是另一题<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:346:<li><b>同一题：</b>同一个结果能同时判两个问题。另一个估计、来源、措辞、方向<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 测试 4</span>；同一总量的另一种人群或代用口径（D190 碰撞裁决提示 collision-v1：\"another population or proxy of one aggregate\"；D197 引的 role-v12 原文：\"another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\"）。候选并进已开问题，用它的结果档和到期日<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。只有以共同量理由开题、带量的候选由代码自动判，其余是匹配和碰撞裁决的判断。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:348:<li><b>同一件事的不同截止日：</b>早的那题开着时，晚的截止日是它的证据，不另开；早的到期没有结果、事情还在追，系统开下一个截止日的续期题，带上并进来的证据，不等新文章<span class=\"src\">D248 第 2 条</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:350:<li><b>公司自己的量：</b>只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据，两种年份差得多时分量低一点<span class=\"src\">D248 第 4 条；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:354:<li><b>约束性义务：</b>\"一笔或一个计划\"一题<span class=\"src\">D210</span>；一笔交易是不是某个已按金额开题的计划的一部分，由匹配判，是就并入<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。还没签的单笔交易是\"签不签\"的是非题，照旧可以开，不并进计划的金额题<span class=\"src\">D210；PRD 06；D248 未改</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:355:<li><b>共同量：</b>以共同量理由开题、带量的候选（量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算），由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判同一题；政策阶段和别的事件保留按事件判的身份；不带这个开题理由的主题量由模型判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:362:<tr><td>测试 1–3、同一篇文章里的测试 4、属于哪一类、问题怎么写</td><td>抽取的模型（判断）</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:363:<tr><td>结果档形状、期间是真日期、到期在文章之后、季度数、年限、约束性义务 18 个月、<code>settled_by</code> 不为空</td><td>代码：只查形状，不判重要性<span class=\"src\">D154、D155、D184</span></td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:408:<h3>5.4 一条记录必须保住的意思<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3，原样</span></h3>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:420:<p>原始发言日不知道就写不知道，不能填报道日<span class=\"src\">D220</span>。一条记录单独读要能懂，条件不能只放在旁边另一条里<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3，引主分支 D251；两个分支的决定编号各自独立，D227</span>。不必要的：转述机构、普通发言场合、付费方案全名；漏了不扣原意分，<b>编造了仍算记录错误</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3</span>。没有来源证实的结论，可以作为分析员的推断写出，但不能写成来源说的事实<span class=\"src\">D218</span>。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:439:<p>分量问\"这条对判断多重要\"，分四级。按投资后果判它碰到的是什么；核心和辅助的界线按信息量定<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §4；D243 第 1 条</span>。缺金额、缺日期只影响分到哪一档，不是不留的理由<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。分量不由数字多不多、是不是官方、库里有没有页、和我们方向是否相同、文章篇幅决定<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §4</span>；离现在远不是不留的理由<span class=\"src\">D216</span>，它落在核心还是辅助由判断定。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:456:<p><b>Alex 拍过的分量</b><span class=\"src\">D215；gold-check.md，D229</span>：收入增速核心；内存短缺核心；AMD 跑分辅助；三条政策辅助；云厂商支出核心；Omniverse 辅助；Sharon \"辅助属于供给需求\"；商谈最多 6000 亿支持 OpenAI 核心（在谈的金额）；投资 SB Energy 15 亿核心；Broadcom AI 半导体收入 +143%、Google Cloud 三个数辅助（别家公司的经营数字）；FY2028 EPS 辅助（远期）；逐案审核、有拒绝辅助（没有量和确定结果）。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:472:<p class=\"note\">下面这份第 3 版金标是历史记录。第 4 版（D248）改了开题的规则，没有改动证据条目（逐条核对见 <span class=\"path\">research/2026-10-30-noise/gold-v4-evidence-check.md</span>）；第 5 版（D250）改了证据的四条界线。金标的证据部分按第 5 版重推，两位互不知情的读者逐条判，分歧对着原文定，另存成新文件冻结，每条改动写改前、改后和理由，第 3 版文件不动（D243 第 11 条）。开题部分要按第 4 版逐条重判，重判之前打分程序不报开题的分；证据部分版本对不上，打分程序拒绝打分（D244、D250）。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:487:<li><b>问题：</b>必须开的（类、开题理由、标的或主题、要点、<code>settled_by</code>）；可以开的（另一种合理写法）；不该开的（第 4 节哪一行或哪个测试）。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:531:<li><b>每一句都对得上这一页。</b>提示词里每一句关于留、不留、分量、开题的话，在这一页找得到出处；找不到的，是给 Alex 的提议，不是改动<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §6</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:572:<li><b>全部文章各发一次，和上一版比</b>改一句会改变每一次请求，所以要发的是全部文章。\"别的版本都留住、只有这一版丢了\"的核心或辅助才算回归信号；单次发送本身每版有 0–4 条这样的意外丢失<span class=\"src\">D243 第 8 条；surprise.py</span>。每个信号读原始答案、问模型自己的理由，追到是不是这次改的那一句造成的。这是诊断。出错的那几篇只用来找机制；接不接受，看全部文章三次发送、和新对照一起报的结果<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §7</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:574:<li><b>一批改完再验收</b>在最终配置上三次发送，按 9.2 由不是作者的读者评，结果给 Alex<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §11</span>。</li>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:605:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D241</td><td class=\"nowrap\">这份标准</td><td>\"几个大类型的账本 - 开题标准和档次 这两个要完整的定义好写好\"；\"档位根据信息量作定标 -以上有你自己trace 过的golden set 来做为改prompt测试标准\"</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:618:<tr><td>B3</td><td>约束性义务：一笔或一个计划一题（D210），还是一组入股是一个判断（D201 规则 G）</td><td>按 D210 \"一笔或一个计划\"；一笔交易属不属于已开的计划，由匹配判；同一计划的几种说法是一题；够不上公司规模的单笔交易不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判</td><td>D210、D236、D238、D248</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:619:<tr><td>B4</td><td>开题测试三套，提示词和代码都没用</td><td>第 1 版 §6 四个测试加评审三条写法检查（第 4 节）；测试 4 和库比的部分归匹配</td><td>第 1 版 §6；评审 §1；D211</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:623:<tr><td>B8</td><td>分量几级、\"档位\"一词两义</td><td>四级；\"档位\"在这一页叫分量，问题的叫结果档</td><td>第 1 版 §10.3；D243 第 1 条</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:624:<tr><td>B9</td><td>几套\"不要\"的类</td><td>抽取只有一套：按 5.3 各行及其边界判，判为不收的分量是\"不收\"；\"不可用\"属于判断这一步（第 7 节）；\"无关陈述\"用定稿金标计数</td><td>第 1 版 §2、§4；D221；D240；D243 第 12 条</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:627:<tr><td>B12</td><td>研究组、驱动层</td><td>研究组不是问题，不代替开题判断；七类驱动是重要性的理由；词汇表只禁 \"thesis driver\"</td><td>D165、D208；评审 §6</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:630:<tr><td>B15</td><td>标的五档必须叫\"非常看多……\"（代码），还是写业务结果（D186）</td><td>这一页按 D186 写；代码是另一模块，D186 未实现照旧记</td><td>D186</td></tr>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:652:<p>新案例上留不留的一致率从第二轮的 80–94% 升到 93–98%，连分量从 72–87% 升到 81–89%。剩下的分歧几乎都在核心和辅助的界线，由 D243 第 1 条定下判法。三位读者判对、作者判错的，记作作者的错：最大客户带来的收入和中国销售占比不该开题（独立意义测试），还有两处陈述。记录在 <span class=\"path\">simulation-log.md</span>。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:655:<p>Codex 只读，逐条对照签过的第 1 版、全部决策、PRD 06，找\"作者自己加的规则\"、和决策矛盾的地方、引错的原话。每一轮的发现都改掉并记下处理。第一轮查出 18 处自己加的规则和 9 处和决策矛盾，比如\"名单外公司的量不开题\"违反 D155、D187，\"抽取要和库里比重复\"违反 D211，把达标线缩短，把\"在谈的金额\"排除出核心。最后三轮只剩措辞层面的问题；第十一轮的发现在 2.14 版改掉，没有再复查。</p>\ndocs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:687:<footer>Hivemind · 抽取与开题标准 · 第 5 版 · 2026-10-29 Alex 签字（D243），2026-10-30 按 Alex 逐个选的七条修订（D248），2026-10-31 按 Alex 定的证据四条界线和计数单位修订（D250）。页首的 standard-version 是规则的版本号：改任何一条规则都要升它，金标随之重定，打分程序遇到版本对不上就拒绝打分（D244）。</footer>\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1330:  只追加 → 只加不改; 一条轴上的结果 → 从一头排到另一头的结果; the module title drops \"thesis · ladder · evidence\";\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1681:- Test small before any full run: \"你最好小范围的测试下不要全部跑完然后完全不 work 或是质量有问题再全部重跑\". The first week, then August: \"你别全跑，到 8 月底先。我们来完整的看下结果\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1683:- Model: gpt-6-luna stays: \"那我觉得还是用 luna 吧，记录这个比较结果\". The comparison with DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 (the `deepseek-flash` endpoint) is in `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`: the only way to get schema-valid JSON from it was a strict tool call with thinking off (3/3; json_object 2/3 and 1/3; thinking-mode forbids a forced tool_choice); about five times cheaper (≈$0.01 against ≈$0.05 per transcript), 18–22 s against 26–31 s, three times more evidence, the candidate set a little less stable; matching and re-judging were not tested on it.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1689:- The window: \"嗯改成 8/15 吧；然后已有的结果封存，然后改一下重判的设置，然后继续跑完剩下的\". The results through the last completed day are sealed in `poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0728/` with `SHA256SUMS`; the same views database continues from the next day to 2026-08-15 with daily re-judging.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2023:- Confirmed by Alex after the 49-probe comparison (5 views mapped per idea against 2, 2,704 input tokens against 27,048): \"可以，你确认这个方向是对的，先定论，然后再继续想要怎么优化 1. 速度 2. 成本 3. 质量和稳定的结果\". The split is the design; what follows is tuning, each change measured against a fresh control on the same ideas.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2221:- Under D153 (Alex: \"T2可以按照你看完T1的结果自己思索之后开始动工…我要看的就是量化的结果收敛\"), the contract of\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2250:- Alex 看过验收审查后要求「好你开始吧，我们一起看」。先修验收定义和离线检查入口，用已存结果及受控反例验证，不把旧关系保留或零次判断报成新归组成功。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2260:- 实测已结束且业务验收失败：20 次调用、估算 $0.373923；三次归组只有一次接回风险判断，仍有错归与错连。实验自身漏传的编号 schema 约束已在原答上修正，未付费复测。原答和结果在 `poc/reports/2026-10-25-ohio-grouping-01/`；关于改变观点入口的建议尚未决定，不启动下一臂。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2269:- D158 运行结果：免费重放 326 个答案，事件年度修复仅恢复 NAVER 一条部署事件及三条证据；两个反向修改和完整 211 项测试通过。在线第一条对照请求 180.342 秒超时，无模型回答；其余五个序列未开始，$0.105535 未知用量保留额不释放。新入口尚无在线效果结论，不推广、不自动重发。结果：`poc/reports/2026-10-25-ohio-grouping-02/results.md`。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2276:- 每个案例每臂三次，最多 24 次请求、$1.50 估算保留额、30 分钟；与 D158 超时请求及其未知费用分开，不自动重发。原文审阅形成的开发预期不是人工金标，结果不充当完整分组验收。前端、Idea、分类、Pull、最终判定和上层论点均不在本次范围。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2277:- 结果：顺序修复的 3 项入口测试、31 项相关测试、完整 214 项套件通过；恢复旧并行的反向修改被调用顺序断言抓住。身份试验的 24 次是草案上限，实际没有开始，生成费用为零。下一步先确认“同问题去重、同项目不同问题归组、原意改变归抽取”的验收界限，再固定最小实验；不得按被审查否决的预期启动。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2285:- D160 实测结果：六个序列全部完成，36 次调用，估算 $0.51142625。新入口三次均把两项融资问题分别保留且归在同组，但风险论据和三种金额口径完整保留均只有 2/3，与对照覆盖相同；完整验收失败，不推广、不自动续开臂。18 条成员、54 次出处交接全部对应；完整 216 项 Python 测试通过。后两篇没有新候选，不能声称检验了旧身份拆分问题。结果和剩余合同问题见 `poc/reports/2026-10-25-ohio-grouping-03/results.md`。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2292:- 实测失败：36 次调用、估算 $0.497585。新角色批评论据 3/3（对照 2/3），但首篇总成本只保留 1/3（对照 0/3），两臂各有一次把 Ohio 问题放进 Rubin 组。11 条成员及 66 次出处交接全部对应，说明错误已在原答，不是保存丢失。217 项测试通过。默认不变，抽取未封存；分两步读内容再建问题的建议尚未决定或实施。结果：`poc/reports/2026-10-25-extraction-evidence-01/results.md`。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2313:- Alex then handed the English library build (D163, [english-library.md](research/2026-10-25-english/english-library.md)) to Claude: \"好那你按照codex 需求来重建，然后开始充分的测试，一定要仔细的看结果以及评量\". The build log with one row per measured step, costs and mistakes is [build-log.md](research/2026-10-25-english/build-log.md).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2523:- Alex: \"太贵了抽 N 次 … 其他的点你自己深度思考啊 … 你深度的研究思考小范围尝试，给我结果让我清晰的做决策\". Sampling several times per item is ruled out on cost.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2596:- Alex, on the arm1 result and the proposal: \"你接着做，需要非常严谨的看结果和测量\". Census first ([labels](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/replacements-47-labels.json), every pair read): of the run's 47 retirements, 22 are the owner's later value or status of the same claim (right under rule E), 20 retired a statement that should have stayed (10 a contradiction or qualification, among them a denial erasing the delay report, \"subject to final agreements\" erasing the $500bn announcement; 10 a different matter), 5 were restatements mislabelled. Jev's `supersedes` label does not separate them: 17 of 22 right and 12 of 20 wrong carry it; with \"confirms or denies\" split out (`jev_contradicts.py`) 4 wrong ones flip to `contradicts` but so do 3 right ones. No label the matcher gives is safe to retire on.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2633:- Alex, on the root cause (\"你还是没有根因的去解决这个问题 … 要么挂不到，要么挂多\"; \"跑那个归档实验\"; \"你看着结果来做\"; \"一样的标准开始测\"). The mechanism ([routing-analysis.md](research/2026-10-28-extraction-quality/routing-analysis.md)): the in-call link decision was a coin flip (36% right on the gold, 46–78 pieces kept from the same bytes) and the gate at once (an unlinked statement was dropped: 60% of all statements, ~15–30% of them material); the link rule routed demand news to the company-wide quantities (six root theses held 66% of all links; v2's pieces 86% double-linked, 26% cited); the thesis list had no driver layer.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2755:- Alex：“那你要改对尺子啊，你现在就改，这个已经错了好几次了，你要把金标准给订好”。本次直接订案，不再把已授权的判断留为待问。范围是 [v4 清单](research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/gold-v4-2026-10-29/reference.md) 的 16 项、11 篇保存来源，全部属于已观察的开发案例；不冒称全周穷尽金标。覆盖 D215 十一题和 D216 EPS 更正，区分用户原话、合并回答的解释、本次模型定级。原始金标和历史结果保留。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2863:- Alex: \"你好好做完这个可以开多个subagent 并行测试，但是要确保控制变量，不要同时改到你要测试的prompt, 快速并行验证给结果\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2917:- Alex, stopping the class-by-class loop: \"你要开始校准，但是整个判断标准和账本类型是不是完全的干净同一？我们今天一直浪费时间在不同标准之间来回 - 几个大类型的账本 - 开题标准和档次 这两个要完整的定义好写好，我们的提示词和测量才会有统一的标准，你停下手边的工作先把我这个事情完整深度的给做好，你必须非常的谨慎来做多次校验逻辑的仿真我们来review\"; then: \"你确定这些足够作作为prd 指引 - 有涵盖我的抽取开题，研究观点标准 -档位根据信息量作定标 -以上有你自己trace 过的golden set 来做为改prompt测试标准 你自己深度review 几轮把这个写好作为这个环节最重要的参考再接着做\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2946:- Decided: role-v51 replaces role-v42; `scripts/replay.py` defaults to `poc/config/poc-v67.json`, which differs from `poc-v58` only in the ten extraction prompt versions (T*-v51). role-v51 changes one clause of the main_driver opening reason to the page's §3 B row (the generation of the company's own product that carries the quantity, its launch or first shipment), with one example and one counter-example (+177 characters). Against role-v42 sent together: must-not questions on small products, features and services 20 → 0 over 15 draws each; one full run (development + test, three draws) shows no cost elsewhere: must-open raised in every draw 18 against 16 of 28, core 235 against 230 of 258, supporting in two draws 154 against 155 of 181, rejected sentences kept 100 against 106 per draw; all paired intervals cross 0 (`loop-log.md` rows 20–22).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2956:- Alex, on the census of duplicate and trivial questions: \"我们的标准要收口\"; then \"你要不要深度的写好plan, 怎么测量，golden 是怎么，我们来解决这个问题；整体不能regress，你要秉持我们过往工程的原则，以及作为一个hedge fund analyst 到底怎么判断合并，去重，这个标准很重要，不能观点爆炸\"; then, not following the plan's table, \"我没理解每个难点，我需要一个一个和你过，你讲人话给我例子\". Each boundary was put to him with an example and two options; his replies are quoted per row. Plan, census and review rounds: [question-identity plan](research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md) §0–§4, §11b, §12.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2960:  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, \"A\"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. Not put to Alex: a not-yet-signed deal's yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart) stays as it is and does not merge into a plan's amount question (the Ohio lease guarantee and the cloud-customer total in v38 both stay). Narrows the standard §4 \"another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)\" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2965:  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, \"A， A\"): a deal, product or project (the question was put about small deals and products) opens a question only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise no question opens, and whether its statement is kept follows the evidence rule (standard §5). Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C (\"a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition\").\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2966:  7. **The same statement carried by several outlets** (H7, \"A\"): code treats pieces with the same known original speaker, original day and figures as one (an unknown speaker or day never matches: 297 of the sealed run's 4,298 pieces have both unknown); the judge sees it once with the outlet count; every piece is still stored. Changes D204's \"both shown to the judge\" for this case, and is a chosen exception to AGENTS §3 \"equal values alone never establish identity\"; the risk put to him with the question (a qualification such as \"excluding China sales\" hidden; D204's 8 of 40 wrong merges) is measured on the G3 gold before it is switched on, as is the accuracy of the original-speaker and original-day fields it relies on.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2967:- Next, in this order: the signed standard page (§3 class C, §4 \"same question, succession or another question\") carries these rules, then a read-only Codex drift review; then the plan's step 1 (structured census, the fixed-extraction replay harness, gold G1–G3, the September holdout week on Alex's go).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3008:- The mechanism (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/plan.md` §3.2′): one placement request, read as the model reads it, held two rulebooks. The system prompt (`placement-narrow-v2`, D207's wording) said a company-wide figure question \"takes only the company's own reported figures, guidance, estimates of that figure and management's statements about it\"; the code-written takes line of the same question said \"figures, guidance, estimates and revisions for <scope> over <period>, and the direct drivers of that figure stated with a size\". The model followed the system prompt: SemiAnalysis's estimate of data-center revenue 3/3 filed under none with the data-center question open, Morgan Stanley's rack price the same, a hyperscaler's own capex guidance 3/3 under none against the hyperscaler-capex question. The system prompt also called filing under none \"a valid answer, not a failure\", and the placer filed 74% of extracted statements nowhere, two fifths of them gold-kept.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3022:- Proposed, not decided (an architecture change was left to Alex on 2026-10-31 and stays his; recording this as decided on the night of 2026-11-01 was an overreach, corrected after his 23:45 message \"你在给我新架构之前有没有想过自己在耍什么智障一直跑一些没用的东西\"; the review is `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md`): the structural cause of the whole class is that one analyst's judgement, \"this statement bears on this bet\", is split across three calls that each hold half the information (extraction has the article and no questions; placement has the questions, a summary and 240 characters of quote; matching only questions). The fix is one decider with the whole article, the day's open questions with their code-written takes lines, and the `links` field defined by that same rule (owner: `placement.takes`'s clauses). It would be extraction version 72 (role-v53's text, the day's open questions shown with takes lines, the links definition in the schema, no separate placement call), one of three ways to give the filing judgement its information (the review §4 lists them with a lean); nothing of it is built or applied until Alex chooses. The 2026-10-31 arm of the same shape (v82, `design-v71-production.md`) failed on two wirings this version does not repeat: its role text halved the candidates (\"only for a matter no open question covers\") and its links bypassed the filing rule.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3026:- Census on one 14-day draw (`e2e-loop/plan.md` §3.8): of 35 declared groups that folded into a stored group by a shared name, 23 carried names the stored group lacked; the Kyber rack group never learnt NVL72x2, Oberon or NVL144 although three articles declared them, so the placer's takes line never showed them and the statements using those names were dropped in every draw.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3032:- Alex, 2026-11-02 00:05, on why questions were duplicated although the matching step sees every open question: \"开题为什么重复？你不是都可以看到存在的题了吗那你操他妈的在干嘛你到底系统有没有接对\"; then \"我刚才说的这个问题你也发现是什么 part of 问题你不该去反思一下这个设计或是哪里有问题直接修直接改。开干。用这个思路来一个一个的提升我们的能力。不要陷入无限没必要的测试循环\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3077:- Alex, 2026-11-02 evening, after asking why the open library was never adopted as the extraction's context (\"你为什么架构上没有采纳我说的开的库作为step 2 context\"; the answer traced the chain from his 10-31 instruction through the one-draw v82 replay I judged \"不采用\" myself to the D256 proposal left waiting): \"我们非常专注的验证这个架构选择：我们有金标和尺子frozen可以比；我们这个架构设计的核心就是透过适当的Prompt 和引入已经开的题，和题的叙述来决定抽取；现在最新的prompt有修改了很多小毛病，你看是不是用最新最好的prompt + v72这边告诉模型怎么用读取开题库的prompt 来做新的实验prompt。充分理解我的ask然后get it worked out\". This is his choice of the one-decider architecture (review-2026-11-02.md §4 way (i), the D256 proposal) and of its base prompt.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3128:- Amended again, 2026-11-02 20:39, after Alex (\"你深度反思为什么分不开，这个完全没有道理啊 … 你根本就是看结果给我讲现象\") and an independent read-only Codex review (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/codex-audit-noise-v94-r1.md`): the \"one dial\" conclusion of the 03:30 amendment is withdrawn as a universal conclusion. A $0 census of the v94 draws against the frozen gold (`harness/noise_by_row_category.py`; `design-v78-fields.md` §11): 107 noise statements over three draws, 31% the standard's \"arrangement in place, no new step\" row, 59% filed under the data-center revenue question, and the company's own publications (T6) yield more noise than kept matter (30 against 19). Defects found in the request and in the field code, none built yet: the role and the check never define what a related party's \"step\" is (any present-tense partner activity counts); the role's \"take it when it has a kind and nothing on the list applies\" contradicts the check's \"fitting a kind does not keep\"; the keep decision attaches to the whole quote; filing is used as the evidence test; the v78–v80 rule rejects a customer's or competitor's judgement for want of scale, against standard kind 3. Alex's product choice of the dial's end is no longer the next task; the next task is the first of the five listed fixes, one at a time, proved on stored articles, and nothing is sent or run until he picks.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3979:  5. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation: PRD 10 is corrected without changing any rule. §4 names the frozen standard's version 5 and\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3983:     statement was found verbatim in the page: \"抽取看不到库\" (§4 and §5.3; changed by D251 and D264), \"研究的交付物是论证\" (§7; the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4025:Alex: “删除金表不一致停止问题；我们要跑完打分；原本的不用跑了吧？结果都有了你combine 一下正确的有帮助/没帮助就可以了；新的prompt测试可以开始打分；你先跑几个看看有没有什么问题”. Remove the gold-inconsistency stop; use the existing frozen gold unchanged and disclose unresolved source/gold concerns alongside scores. D372 combines existing core and supporting as helpful, not-kept as not helpful, and optional remains neutral. Reuse the old stored results where the input and scoring context actually match; first run a few new split-prompt cases, then inspect source, output and failures. This does not adjudicate the three disputed question entries or alter gold, prior scores, the unit, production configuration, or deployment.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4099:  once like a format failure. Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §39.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4124:  out under D382. Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §36.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4131:  entries golden-v5 marks supporting are disclosed as a known conflict with every score (D373). Record: LOG §39.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4138:  built. Record: LOG §39.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4153:  On dev ×3: helpful 214, 211 and 212 of 234. Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §§40–44 and\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4168:  Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §47.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4181:  asks it. Arm c9 showed that a sentence-level rule flips by send (round log §§48–50).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4261:  证据更准”。但真实产品是从零开始自己开题的，这一点这次没测到。下一步做什么？\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4285:  - Alex: \"放下这题，去测自己开题\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4297:- **Asked**, with `clean-arch/unseeded-2026-11-10/MATCHING-v2.md` frozen: \"要不要花钱正式测“新系统自己开题”（只按产品该开的 7 道题打分）？\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4368:  passed two readers (round log §69): \"事件题如果不止“是/否”两种结果（例如监管调查的结局），你定的老规矩是分五种状态。我手写三次都有遗漏或重叠；后来在给模型的请求里加了一个通用做法（先分出互斥的几种结果，如“通过／未决／否决”，再把其中一两种按“是或否”的性质一分为二，并附一个并购审查的例子），按它写的 3 个才通过两位读者。但这个做法没有你定过的任何规矩做依据，按规定要你批准才能写进提示词。怎么办？\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4472:  - Options: one last send and then build (recommended): \"新组合：最初那版 + 已验证不伤拒绝的两句（引用照抄、问题能独立看懂）+ 两种格子，不要“先列主线”那一栏。8 题各 3 次并带对照，约 3 美分。达线就用它写程序；不达线就退回最初那版、写法毛病全交给程序打回。无论结果都不再试发，直接写程序。\"; go back to the first request now and let the checks send answers back; split the step into two calls; stop and read the answers himself.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4505:  - Options: three outcomes (recommended): \"发生了 / 明确落空（被否决、被放弃）/ 到期还没结果。第三种由程序写成“前两种都不是”，所以不会有遗漏。保住了“否决”和“还在等”的区别；更细的区别（如“附条件批准”）列为“不判”。这是我的建议，写法还要先免费验证。\"; yes or no only (the simplest; \"rejected\" and \"still waiting\" become one No, which the council held loses a difference an analyst cares about); several outcomes where they are needed, the number not fixed (the council's recommendation; a new structure, one more round of design).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4571:  - Options: code sets it (recommended): \"公司财年结束后 60 天（美国大公司年报的法定期限）、行业日历年结束后 90 天（约定值）。回放结果 34 道里 32 道一致。代价：公司年报类的题比模型估的日子晚约一个月结案；行业数据偶尔可能比 90 天更晚；不是整年的数字（滚动 12 个月的调查、季度数）不能套这条规则，要先单独处理。\"; as now (the test still fails under line 6 and the work stays at this step).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4606:## D417 · 2026-11-10 · A figure for a rolling twelve months with no publication day in the texts is declined\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4632:- **Decided:** as D415, for the changes of D416, D417 and D418: each is proved small and reviewed in the council; when all pass\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4641:  - Options: it is ruled out (recommended): \"题目保持原样，问的仍是“有没有公布结论”。这类题固定有三种结果：公布了／当局正式放弃且没有结论／还在查。这也是目前多数已存答案的写法，且符合现有规则“判题目点名追踪的那件事”。不写“明确落空”的答案将算错。\"; ask instead whether the investigation is over (two outcomes; it tracks another event than the conclusion the thesis names).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4655:- **Decided:** D417 goes into the working request. Then, each beside the working request and on its own: (a) D420's rule in the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4666:  - Options: the small test of a second look (recommended): \"只是候选做法，不是已证明的修法。通过条件事先写死：18 份公认有错的至少改好 9 份，且 30 份没错的最多改坏 1 份；第二遍的答案若过不了程序检查就沿用第一遍。改过的答案由两类读者盲读。通过也只说明“值得带着它再正式测一次”，不等于六条线过了。若采用，每道新题多一次请求，约多花 0.1 美分和 10 到 20 秒。做完我把结果报给你，再由你定是否采用。\"; go on class by class (the unjustified declines first); open Stage B on the step as it stands (his to waive his lines); stop.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4714:  - Options: not adopted (recommended): \"按事先写死的标准它没通过，我和评审一致。这一步保持第四次正式测试时的样子，不加这次复查。\"; adopt it and run a formal test with it (about $0.3, an estimate); a second look kept to refusals alone (\"评审认为这是看了结果才挑出来的子集，不足以作为下一步\").\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4724:  - Options: prepare the second stage first (recommended): \"不再修这一步，带着已知的这几处错往下走，去量它对最终判断的影响。先只做不花钱的一步：读者盲读已存的 159 条旧判断，建立老判断程序的基准；结果报给你，任何付费测试前再问你。这不等于第一段过线了。\"; go on mending the step class by class and send a fifth Stage A; go back to the gaps upstream (question opening without seeds, capital spending) first; stop here.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4774:  - Options: build it and run once the review clears (recommended): \"补程序、测试、送评审；评审挑不出严重问题就直接发三轮付费测试，不再问你。每条判断单独读，和基准的读法一样，两者才能直接比。读完把结果报给你。第一段没过线这一点会写在每份报告里。\"; build, then ask again; build and read by question packet; stop.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4798:  - Options: current production (recommended): \"双方都不预设题目，条件相同；用冻结的标准、同一天、各跑三轮。“可评分的 7 道题”的结果单独列出。\"; the seeded version with 22 preset questions (\"新系统每轮天然少约 11 道公司财务指标题，几乎不可能赢\"); the seven graded questions only.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4809:  - Options: diagnose how Step 1 cuts theses first (recommended): \"逐篇对照自己开题时漏掉的 9 道标准题、8 个没出题的论点和第一段剩下的错，找出共同原因；再提一个改法，作为第 1 步的新版本，在没用过的新文章上测。开工前会把诊断结果和改法报给你。\"; mend the ladder step's remaining faults (would lift D426's freeze); capital spending (q12) first.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4819:- **Asked**, after the D432 diagnosis (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/DIAGNOSIS.md`, version 8; seven council rounds): \"第 1 步漏开题，最大的一类是：同一个数只开一年 … 我建议只改这两句，加约 150 个字元，不删任何东西。要不要开一个第 1 步的新版本（c14）来试？\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4834:  - Options: finish diagnosing Step 1's other defects, then change them together (recommended): \"先不再改提示词。零花费查清'结果里塞第二样东西'那一类……把这一类、分年、'客户开支'那句的冲突，各自在存档上小证明后，合成一个第 1 步新版本，在没用过的新文章上和 c8 比一次。方案先报给你。\"; c15 (c14 plus the customer-spending sentence) on fresh articles; accept c14's effect and run the controls; stop here.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4859:- **Asked**, with `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate1/G1A-READING.md` and `G1B-READING.md`: \"第一关的结果：'客户那句'的改动过了；'今年明年各开一题'没过。…新版 9 次里只有 5 次把两年分开开题，事先定的线是 9 次至少 8 次。旧版 c8 是 0 次。…新写法 26 次里 20 次分开，旧版 26 次里 0 次。没分开的那几次，模型都读到了规则，但觉得'两年都开太多了'，只留一年。下一步怎么走？\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4860:  - Options: carry both changes to gate 2 (recommended by Claude): \"分年虽然没达线，但从 0 次升到大约四分之三，而且'两年塞一题'完全消失，没发现带坏别的东西。第二关在存档上查它会不会弄坏周边情况（重复文章、同一量的另一种口径、延期的事等，约 1.5 美元，线先给你看）。代价：等于在看到结果后放宽了我自己定的线。\"; stop the year change and carry only the customer sentence (the reviewer, `council/lx-codex.md`, recommended stopping the year change and keeping c8); stop both and keep c8.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5058:  p1) are phase 10's own blocker and in its scope (PRD 10 §§1–3), that opening is out of phase 10 (§3) and needs its distinct mechanisms\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5120:  against total) and q18 (the later Kyber deadline) by §4's same-question rule and the opening tests; q05 by the source, what the system kept\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5154:  Step 1 request settles thesis identity with §4's general rule only, while the clean architecture gives that decision to Step 1 (no later\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5155:  thesis comparison) and §4's boundaries were written for matching; F1 (the unsigned deal beside the plan's amount) and F2 (another year of\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5175:- **Decided:** F6 is not tested on its own; its correction, with the date safeguards of round 8 (no invented release day; D417 intact), waits\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5320:- **Council** (`mu-codex-11.md` to `mu-codex-13.md`): the period candidate is sourced (§3 D \"自然年的今年或明年\") but must protect a comparison with the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5342:- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-15.md`): \"c17 按预定条件失败，不采用；停止在这些文章上继续调整 Step 1 的句子，报告实测结果和暂定选择，并由\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5380:  D417's rolling windows not); only then are they shown the thesis and say whether one of theirs is the same matter and what it loses.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
